---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
/*
  PERSONALIZE THIS PAGE before launch. Real names, a photo, and your family's
  real baseball experience are what make an affiliate site trustworthy (and
  they are what Google's "experience" signals look for). Replace every [bracketed] note.
*/
---
<Base title="About Us" description={`${site.name} is a free gear guide for baseball parents, started as a kid’s idea and built by a baseball family.`}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap-narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">About {site.name}</p>
      <h1>A kid’s idea, built by a baseball family</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {site.name} started with a question from our kid: “What if there was a website that told parents exactly what baseball stuff to buy?”
      </p>
      <p>
        If you’ve stood in the baseball aisle holding two bats that look identical except for a tiny stamp, wondering whether 10½ or 11 inches is right, and whether RHT
        means the glove goes on the right hand (it doesn’t), you know why. Gear for a first season is confusing, the rules change by league and age, and it’s easy to
        spend more than you need to.
      </p>
      <p>
        So we built the guide we wished we’d had: answer a few questions about your kid, and it walks you through every piece of gear, with the exact size, why it
        matters, how to check the fit, and what you can skip.
      </p>
      <p><em>[Add your family’s story here: who you are, how many seasons you’ve been through, positions your kids play, the shopping mistake that started it all. A real photo helps a lot.]</em></p>

      <h2>How we make recommendations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Fit and rules first.</strong> Sizes come from manufacturer charts and league rulebooks, checked against what actually works for real kids.</li>
        <li><strong>We cite our sources.</strong> Every guide links to the official rules we used, and we re-check them every season.</li>
        <li><strong>We tell you what to skip.</strong> A first-year player doesn’t need a $300 bat. We’ll say so.</li>
        <li><strong>Your info stays yours.</strong> The gear guide runs in your browser. We never see your kid’s name or measurements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we make money</h2>
      <p>
        Some shopping links are affiliate links. If you buy through them, the store pays us a small commission at no extra cost to you. That’s what keeps the site free.
        It never changes our sizing advice. <a href="/disclosure/">Read our full disclosure</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Spot something wrong?</h2>
      <p>League rules change. If you notice something out of date, please email us at <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> and we’ll fix it.</p>

      <div style="margin-top:3rem"><CtaBand track="about_cta" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
